WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
1: All About Me and My Family.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.800
Welcome to your first unit of Year 3 English!

3
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.600
In this unit you will learn how to
talk about yourself and your family,

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.020
and about the good values that hold a family and
a school together — respect, honour, and duty.

5
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.940
You will learn how to behave well in public and in
private, and how to talk about health and safety.

6
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.300
By the end, you will be ready to introduce
your family and share what matters to you,

7
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.940
just like Musa does in this unit's story.

8
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.960
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:44.240
By the end of this unit, you will be able to talk about
the people in your family and what you do together.

10
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.500
you will also use new words like
respect, honour, duty, health, and safety.

11
00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.120
you will also say what is happening now,
using the present continuous (“i am helping.”).

12
00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.080
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:05.620
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
family, parent, friend, student, junior, senior.

14
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.700
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:15.360
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.000
The reading sequence includes My
Family and Good Behaviour at School.

17
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.700
Read actively.

18
00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:26.880
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.760
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:36.040
The first language focus is Present
Continuous (what is happening now).

21
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.160
We use the present continuous to talk
about actions that are happening right now.

22
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:47.000
It helps us say exactly what people are doing at
this moment, like “The student is showing respect.”

23
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:53.780
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.560
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Introduce Your Family.

25
00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:03.860
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.540
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.980
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.440
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:18.800
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.520
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.240
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
